Description: cham3 desktop plus the curated application suite (M1)
 Metapackage for the cham3 M1 desktop image. It installs cham3-desktop and the
 curated suite: from Debian 13 (trixie) nmap with Zenmap, masscan,
 bind9-dnsutils, whois, Wireshark and tshark, tcpdump, nethogs, iftop, sqlmap,
 nikto, ffuf, gobuster, aircrack-ng, binwalk, exiftool, hashcat, john, hydra
 and the Tor Browser launcher; and, from two separately authenticated and
 pinned sources, LibreWolf, OWASP ZAP (zaproxy), amass, exploitdb
 (searchsploit), ghidra and radare2. nikto comes from the Debian non-free
 archive area and torbrowser-launcher from contrib.
 .
 Non-Debian members (owner-approved). librewolf comes from the official
 LibreWolf repository. zaproxy, amass, exploitdb, ghidra and radare2 come from
 the Kali archive through a per-package allowlist: those five plus the
 Kali-only libraries libpostal-data, libradare2-6.0.0t64 and
 libradare2-common, and nothing else. Each source has its own pinned key and
 its own apt preferences; every other package of these two repositories has
 priority -1, so they can neither add to nor replace Debian packages. The
 sources, keys and pins belong to the cham3 image definition (build/live-desktop
 in the source tree), not to this package: installing cham3-full on another
 system needs the same sources and pins. Recommends are not installed (for
 example the Kali-only ghidra-data).
 .
 Deferred, pending separate review and NOT dependencies of this package:
 mitmproxy, wpscan and metasploit-framework. The alternatives cutter and
 rizin are omitted in favour of radare2, and burpsuite in favour of zaproxy
 (OWASP ZAP). Until the deferred tools are resolved the image has no
 mitmproxy, no WordPress scanner and no exploitation framework.
 .
 Package presence is not a safety or isolation claim. Installing this
 metapackage does not sandbox any tool, apply a permission contract or enforce
 a network mode; those features do not exist in M1.
